<p>In the latest development in the Iran war, President Trump said the United States is &quot;not putting troops&quot; into the Middle East, seeking to reassure Americans as the conflict nears its third week and fresh Iranian attacks hit energy facilities in the Gulf. The new strikes rattled oil markets and pushed prices higher, extending the conflict’s economic impact beyond the battlefield. Trump also said he would do whatever was necessary to lower oil prices, while Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth said the administration remained on track and that the President would decide when to stop the war. Together, the developments suggest a U.S. effort to project control and avoid a wider ground deployment even as attacks on Gulf energy infrastructure add pressure on global supply and regional diplomacy.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/18JhwuWQSQvPV5rpJmfOdcvXkhKkyrJCIcNXtA7z7v7UkW-baSxkXNlG_f9FfTicEWw8OQopmas1YIG1lTAp8Re6CPy14N2xova2KEcZsYqp5AinLDTmog-0Xwvb92SHzyN3Hj8z5ucgzMGlDoa-3PauOmBAFq6t-U1M6cVLZehpnfNqdMPODfJhWpYgS5__KnE09VDzJYv1XDHYwsXMrOVeKO4UKbKmRzPtkuaQBjI_PzC_9lHA0zoHjhVBBcYg0NUy9wxqnsFITCNiWg' alt='Israeli soldiers stand next to a fragment of a missile fired from Iran in the Israeli-controlled Golan Heights on Thursday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>White House setting: Trump made the remark during a White House meeting with Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi.</li><li>Direct question: He made the no-troops comment when asked whether he was planning to send soldiers to the Middle East.</li><li>Infrastructure exchange: The latest round included Iran hitting Gulf refineries after Israeli strikes on Iran’s offshore gas field, showing that both sides are targeting economically sensitive energy assets.</li></ul><blockquote>I&#x27;m not putting troops anywhere - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: As oil reached new highs after the Gulf strikes, he stressed bringing prices down and framed the conflict partly through its effect on U.S. consumers. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/19/world/iran-war-news-trump-oil'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth: His comments signaled that the Pentagon sees the campaign as going according to plan while leaving the decision on when it ends to President Trump. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/19/qatar-expels-officials-from-irans-embassy-after-attacks-on-ras-laffan-gas-field'>Euronews</a>)</li><li>Qatar: By expelling Iranian embassy officials after the Ras Laffan attack, Doha showed that Gulf governments were responding with diplomacy as well as security measures. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/19/qatar-expels-officials-from-irans-embassy-after-attacks-on-ras-laffan-gas-field'>Euronews</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-iran-hits-gulf-refineries-after-israeli-strikes-its-offshore-gas-field/'>Iran intensifies attacks on Gulf neighbours, spiking global oil prices</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/19/qatar-expels-officials-from-irans-embassy-after-attacks-on-ras-laffan-gas-field'>Trump says he is &#x27;not putting troops&#x27; in Iran as war continues for almost three weeks</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/19/world/iran-war-news-trump-oil'>Iran War Live Updates: As Attacks Rattle Markets, Trump Seeks to Reassure Americans</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/trump-says-not-putting-us-troops-in-region-amid-iran-war'>Trump says US is not putting troops in Middle East region</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/trump-says-not-putting-us-troops-region-amid-iran-war'>Trump says not putting US troops in region amid Iran war</a> - al-monitor.com</li></ul>